 "source_contradictions": [
  "Throughput claim: the decision guide Aurora row says 'up to five times the throughput of standard MySQL'; CHAP_AuroraOverview says 'up to 6x the throughput of stock PostgreSQL and up to 6x ... stock MySQL'. Not recorded as a fact by this lens.",
  "Global Database size: the DR whitepaper says 'up to five secondary Region'; the Aurora user guide and the May 2025 post say up to 10 secondary Regions. The guide is current; the whitepaper is old.",
  "Aurora serverless minimum: the guide and the November 2024 post say 0 ACUs; the Aurora pricing page worked example still says the minimum database capacity you can set is 0.5 ACUs.",
  "Encryption default date: the What's New post is dated Feb 16, 2026 ('starting today'); the user guide says clusters created on or after February 18, 2026.",
  "Free tier storage unit: aurora-free-tier says up to 1 GB; the pricing page and FAQ say 1 GiB.",
  "Deleted-cluster backups: the Aurora FAQ says automated backups are not kept after an instance is deleted; since August 4, 2023 you can retain automated backups for a deleted cluster (history row and What's New post).",
  "Serverless scale to zero: two history rows (July 25, 2024 and November 20, 2024). The What's New post and the version table in the guide point to November 2024; the July row has no distinguishing text."
 ],
